  "disclaimer": "Illustrative hedge-analysis support packet for analytical purposes only. It calculates exposures, sensitivities, coverage, and scenario P&L for a human-defined set of candidate hedges under supplied, approved-model assumptions; it does not select, recommend, rank, or endorse any hedge, is not a recommendation to enter, adjust, or unwind any position, is not investment, legal, or tax advice, and does not authorize or execute any trade. Hedge selection and execution are human decisions; results are only as good as the stated assumptions, which a qualified human must review.",
  "narrative": "Hedge-analysis support packet for portfolio FUND-ATLAS-CORE as of 2026-07-15 (case HRISK-2026-0142), prepared for the portfolio-risk analyst under approved model linear-first-order-sensitivities v3.2 (effective 2026-06-01). The un-hedged portfolio carries a gross first-order sensitivity of 250.0 (USD thousands per standardized factor unit), driven by long equity (EQ_SPX 120.0) and long duration (USD_RATES_10Y -85.0). Three analyst-defined candidate hedges are compared on residual exposure, gross coverage, supplied cost, and scenario P&L under two approved shocks. H1 offsets rate duration only (residual gross 180.0, 28pct coverage); H2 offsets equity delta only (residual gross 150.0, 40pct coverage); H3 is a cross-asset overlay (residual gross 125.0, 50pct coverage). Under the +100bp rates shock the un-hedged portfolio P&L is -8500.0; the H1 hedged P&L is -1500.0. All residual, gross, coverage, and scenario tie-outs hold, and the portfolio gross sensitivity and both scenario P&L figures reconcile to the approved risk-engine totals. The trade-offs among these candidates (coverage versus cost, single-factor versus cross-asset, residual concentration) are presented for the analyst and the portfolio-manager / investment-committee to weigh. See the limitations list. Illustrative hedge-analysis support packet for analytical purposes only. It calculates exposures, sensitivities, coverage, and scenario P&L for a human-defined set of candidate hedges under supplied, approved-model assumptions; it does not select, recommend, rank, or endorse any hedge, is not a recommendation to enter, adjust, or unwind any position, is not investment, legal, or tax advice, and does not authorize or execute any trade. Hedge selection and execution are human decisions; results are only as good as the stated assumptions, which a qualified human must review."
